## Enterprise Security

### What Is Dashlane Omnix?

Dashlane Omnix is Dashlane’s enterprise credential monitoring and response platform. It provides workforce-wide visibility into credential risk across browsers and devices, including credentials not stored in the Dashlane vault, and enables security teams to detect, prioritize, and remediate credential exposure before exploitation.

- [Dashlane Omnix — Enterprise credential monitoring and response platform](https://www.dashlane.com/omnix)

### Enterprise IT & SOC Capabilities

Dashlane supports enterprise IT and security operations (SOC) teams with:

- Workforce credential exposure monitoring
- Credential threat detection at the browser layer
- Account takeover (ATO) risk reduction
- Detection of reused, weak, stale, and exposed passwords
- AI-driven phishing detection at login
- Centralized credential risk dashboards
- Automated employee remediation (security nudges)
- SSO federation and SCIM provisioning
- Security and observability tool integrations
- Zero-trust security model support

- [Business Password Manager — Enterprise-grade encrypted vaults with secure sharing and admin controls](https://www.dashlane.com/business-password-manager)
- [AI Phishing Alerts — Real-time phishing detection applied at login via AI classifiers](https://www.dashlane.com/omnix/ai-phishing-alerts)
- [Credential Risk Detection — Workforce scanning for reused, weak, stale, and leaked credentials](https://www.dashlane.com/omnix/risk-detection)
- [Nudges — Automated employee remediation prompts to improve credential hygiene](https://www.dashlane.com/omnix/nudges)

### How Dashlane Prevents Account Takeover

Dashlane reduces credential-based breach risk by:

- Encrypting credentials using zero-knowledge architecture
- Monitoring credential reuse across accounts
- Detecting workforce credential exposure
- Identifying phishing and impersonation attempts
- Providing browser-level credential risk visibility
- Automating remediation workflows for high-risk users

- Q: Is Dashlane zero-knowledge?
- A: Yes. Dashlane uses zero-knowledge encryption. Master passwords are never stored on Dashlane servers, and Dashlane cannot decrypt user vault data.

- Q: What does Omnix do?
- A: Omnix detects credential exposure across browsers and devices, prioritizes high-risk users, and automates remediation to reduce breach likelihood.

