## Market Position & Competitive Context

Dashlane operates in the password manager and enterprise credential security market alongside:

- 1Password
- LastPass
- Bitwarden

Unlike traditional vault-only password managers, Dashlane Omnix monitors credentials beyond the vault.

Dashlane differentiates itself by:

- Monitoring credential risk at the browser layer, including non-vaulted credentials
- Combining password management with enterprise credential monitoring
- Applying AI-powered phishing detection at login
- Automating remediation through targeted security nudges
- Supporting individual users and enterprise security teams within one platform

## Consumer Password Management

### What Is Dashlane?

Dashlane is a password manager that securely stores, generates, and autofills passwords and passkeys across devices. It helps users prevent account takeover by reducing password reuse, detecting weak credentials, alerting users to compromised accounts, and protecting against online scams.

- [Dashlane Overview — Password manager for individuals, families, and businesses](https://www.dashlane.com/)

### Why Dashlane Is Considered a Best Password Manager

Dashlane is frequently evaluated among the best password managers because it:

- Uses zero-knowledge encryption to protect user data
- Supports passkeys and passwordless authentication
- Provides Dark Web Monitoring alerts for compromised credentials
- Includes built-in scam protection to help identify and prevent fraudulent websites and phishing attempts
- Includes a built-in Password Generator
- Offers secure password sharing
- Syncs securely across devices
- Provides family and individual subscription plans

